# Server Action clipboard workflow

Write or edit the action under the selected temporary directory, then copy it with the platform clipboard tool or copy the file manually. Do not treat `pbcopy` as universal.

## Copy the action body

- macOS: `pbcopy < "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}.py"`
- Windows PowerShell: `Get-Content -Raw "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}.py" | Set-Clipboard`
- Linux Wayland: `wl-copy < "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}.py"`
- Linux X11: `xclip -selection clipboard < "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}.py"`

## Save the copied output

- macOS: `pbpaste > "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}_output.txt"`
- Windows PowerShell: `Get-Clipboard | Set-Content -Encoding utf8 "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}_output.txt"`
- Linux Wayland: `wl-paste > "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}_output.txt"`
- Linux X11: `xclip -selection clipboard -o > "{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}_output.txt"`

If no clipboard tool exists, open `{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}.py`, copy it manually, then paste the Odoo modal or notification output into `{{ temp_dir }}/{{ action_file }}_output.txt`.

Parse JSON with uv-managed Python. Save this helper as `{{ temp_dir }}/parse_action_output.py`, then run `uv run --script "{{ temp_dir }}/parse_action_output.py" "{{ temp_dir }}" "{{ action_file }}"`:

```python
import json
import sys
from pathlib import Path

temp_dir = Path(sys.argv[1])
action_file = sys.argv[2]
text = (temp_dir / f'{action_file}_output.txt').read_text(encoding='utf-8').strip()
payload = json.loads(text)
(temp_dir / f'{action_file}_output.json').write_text(
    json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2),
    encoding='utf-8',
)
print(json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
```
